# rena0-hyper-ex-camera — F1-3 fixture, the Hyper EX attack's action camera
#
# Source: FUN_0043ffc0 case 0x15e (the EX body, move 350) writes the actor's camera-request
# word itself (:1437-1442): set 0 for the whole move, and set 1 from tick 0x33 only when the
# late-window hit latch is set. The request has NO contact test around it, so the base
# cinematic plays on a whiff too — the owner confirmed that against the original's own
# screenshot. This fixture pins the whiff path: set 0 (V3-37).
#
# The opponent sits 2000 units away, so the EX swing cannot connect: `attack_row 350` and a
# non-zero `action_camera` on the same tick prove the camera is not a hit effect.
combo 0 0
seed 5489
spawn 0 0 0 0
spawn 1 0 0 2000
collision open-field
hyper oyashiro
input 0 SPECIAL
input 1 -
input 20 SPECIAL
input 21 -
expect 0 hyper 1
# -1 is "no action camera"; 0 is the rig's first set, which is what this move requests.
expect 19 action_camera -1
# The press tick already runs the move's first program update, so the camera arms there.
expect 20 attack_row 350
expect 20 action_camera 0
expect 30 action_camera 0
expect 30 swing_hits 0
